// CreateAgentWithBodyWithResponse Create an agent and start its AI coding agent
//
// Without project, the agent belongs to the project whose worktree
// holds dir, and starts there. With it, in dir when dir is in the
// project, else in the project's clone path. With parent, it is a child
// of that agent: it belongs to the parent's project and starts in the
// parent's dir, whatever dir is.
//
// With worktree, it starts in that worktree of the project instead:
// "main" is the clone, any other name matches the base name of a
// worktree's path. A name that matches none creates the worktree in
// <project root>/.worktrees/<name>, on a new branch of that name from the
// HEAD of where it would otherwise start, and excludes .worktrees from
// git unless git already ignores it. A worktree created stays when the
// agent then fails, and the next request finds it.
//
// With model, its AI coding agent is told to use that model, and with
// permissions it may do that without asking; both are kept for every
// later start. A model with whitespace or a control character, or longer
// than 200 bytes, is invalid_argument; nothing else about it is checked.
//
// With aca, it runs that AI coding agent, which must be installed and
// enabled (listAcas); by default the first that is. One the daemon does not
// know is not_found with details.argument aca; one not installed or
// disabled, or none to run, is aca_unavailable, with details.aca,
// details.reason (not_installed or disabled) and details.program, null
// when none was asked for.
//
// An agent that does not start is left failed and returns start_failed
// with the agent under details.agent.
//
// Errors: aca_unavailable, agent_removed, branch_exists, invalid_argument, invalid_name,
// invalid_path, name_taken, not_found, path_exists, project_closed,
// start_failed, worktree_failed.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/agents (the `CreateAgent` operationId).
